    "standardized_narrative": "At 1 January 2021 Syndicate 1414 carried gross claims outstanding of GBP 722.4m. During 2021 there was an aggregate gross adverse prior-year development of approximately GBP 66.1m (c.9.1% of opening reserves), i.e. a strengthening of reserves driven largely by adverse development on older catastrophe losses (notably Hurricane Laura and the 2010 New Zealand earthquake). After reinsurance the syndicate reports a net run-off deficit on prior accident years of GBP 32.2m, split between reinsurance acceptance business (GBP 23.1m) and direct business (GBP 9.1m). The 2021 current-year catastrophes (Winter Storm Uri, European Floods, Hurricane Ida, US Tornados and Amplify Energy) also materially affected the year's claims experience.",
